## Map engine architecture

```
MainActivity (mapEngine = MapLibreEngineImpl())
  └── DashboardScreen(mapEngine)
        └── CarMapViewContainer(engine)
              ├── AndroidView → MapLibreEngineImpl.createMapView()
              ├── HUD from engine.uiState.collectAsState()
              └── NavigationSearchOverlay → searchDestination() / navigateToCoordinates()
```

- Style: inline OSM raster JSON (`tile.openstreetmap.org`) — not `demotiles.maplibre.org` (no PH coverage)
- Routing: `routing.openstreetmap.de/routed-car` OSRM API (not `router.project-osrm.org` — returns 403); `User-Agent: MixAutoCarLauncher/1.0` required; route line via GeoJsonSource + LineLayer `#00CBD6`
- Search: Nominatim with `User-Agent: MixAutoCarLauncher/1.0`
- Location: `MapLibreFusedLocationEngineImpl` (AOSP, no Google Services dep); runtime `ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION` + `ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION` both requested
- MapLibre version pinned **11.5.1** in `gradle/libs.versions.toml` — 11.7.0 caused emulator RenderThread SIGSEGV with location puck + vector Liberty + TomTom traffic; validate on physical head unit before any SDK bump
- **Rotation / config change:** `MainActivity` has no `configChanges` — activity recreates on orientation change; **ViewModels survive**; do NOT recreate `MapLibreEngineImpl` in `onCreate` — use activity-scoped **`MapHostViewModel`** (`ui/map/MapHostViewModel.kt`) holding `mapEngine`, `navigationVoiceController`, `localPlacesRepository`; teardown only in `MapHostViewModel.onCleared()` — **do NOT** call `engine.onDestroy()` from `CarMapViewContainer` lifecycle (`ON_DESTROY` removed)

## MapView / lifecycle

- MapView lifecycle race: `DisposableEffect` calls `onStart`/`onResume` before `AndroidView` factory runs — call `view.onStart()`/`view.onResume()` in `createMapView()` after `onCreate(null)`
- MapLibre 11.x removed `LocationEngineProvider` — use `LocationEngineProxy(AndroidLocationEngineImpl(ctx))` for emulator compatibility
- `CarMapViewContainer` needs `lifecycle-runtime-compose` for `LocalLifecycleOwner`
- Cached `MapView` in `MapLibreEngineImpl.createMapView()`: detach from parent via `(parent as? ViewGroup)?.removeView()` before returning to a new `AndroidView`
- Do not call `engine.onDestroy()` in `CarMapViewContainer` composable `onDispose` — only forward `ON_DESTROY` from activity lifecycle; layout changes remove/re-add the composable but must keep the map engine alive

## Location / GPS / puck

- Map loads before location permission dialog — `MainActivity` must call `retryLocationActivation()` when permission already granted, not only after dialog
- Emulator mock GPS: `getLastKnownLocation` often null until `requestLocationUpdates(GPS_PROVIDER, …)` fires; refresh on `onResume` after Extended Controls changes
- Emulator GPS (`adb emu geo fix`, Extended Controls) delivers 0 location reports on some AVDs — this is an AVD-level failure, not an app bug; test location on a physical device
- `MapLibreEngineImpl` registers GPS location listener ONCE via `listenersRegistered` flag — do not tear down and re-register on every `onResume`; rapid re-registration causes AppOps `op=GPS: Operation not started` errors and no fixes are delivered
- `forceLocationUpdate(location)` on `locationComponent` is required to push fixes into MapLibre's blue dot; store fix in `pendingLocationFix` if component not yet activated, flush in `activateLocationTracking()`
- `navigateToCoordinates()` falls back to map camera center (`resolveMapViewOrigin()`) when GPS is null and camera zoom ≥ 10 — allows routing on emulator without GPS fix
- Use `RenderMode.GPS` (not `COMPASS`) for heading-up driving view; set on `activateLocationTracking()` and before nav/free-drive camera modes
- Synthetic bearing in `MapLibreEngineImpl.enrichLocationWithBearing()`: when `hasBearing()` is false (emulator/mock GPS), compute heading from previous fix via `bearingTo()` if movement > 10 m — prevents north-up camera when moving without compass bearing
- Bearing freeze when stopped: `enrichLocationWithBearing()` treats stopped as speed < `STOPPED_SPEED_MPS` (1.4 m/s) **or** movement < `STOPPED_MOVE_M` (8 m) between fixes; `resolveFrozenBearing()` locks to `lastStableBearing` or current map camera bearing — **must** feed LocationComponent via `BearingEnrichedLocationEngine` wrapper (`createLocationEngine()`); enriching only in `applyAndroidLocation()` does not affect puck/camera because raw engine still drives MapLibre; app speed/HUD listens on `rawLocationEngine`, enriched engine only for LocationComponent activation
- Puck smoothing (2026-06): `SmoothingLocationEngine` speed-adaptive blend (500/700/900 ms default) + extrapolation up to `EXTRAPOLATION_MAX_MS` (2500 ms) / `EXTRAPOLATION_MAX_M` (50 m) between GPS fixes feeds LocationComponent — no per-tick `forceLocationUpdate()`; `setMaxAnimationFps(MAX)` on tracking engage; bearing EMA (`BEARING_EMA_ALPHA`); `resetSmoothingMotion()` on camera detach, top-down, route overview, style reload; high-speed rubber-band often = display ran ahead via extrapolation then snapped on next fix (`resolveBlendStart`) — classify before retuning companions; **do not increase** `EXTRAPOLATION_MAX_*` or snap-back as a first rubber-band move (usually worsens ahead-then-snap)
- Puck flicker fix (2026-07): single GPS subscription — `BearingEnrichedLocationEngine.onRawFix` tees HUD/nav to `onLocationFixForAppLogic()`; do NOT add second `requestLocationUpdates` on `rawLocationEngine`; while `shouldSmoothPuckMotion()` skip `forceLocationUpdateForImmediateRender` (slider path uses `allowDuringSmoothing=true` + `currentDisplayLocation()`); bucketed lookahead padding (`LOOKAHEAD_ENTER/EXIT`, 8 dp quantize); `handleMapLayoutChange` only reapplies padding when key changes; `activateFreeDriveTrackingMode` mode-change only; road-snap hysteresis (`SNAP_TO_ROUTE_RELEASE_M` 45 m); suppress bearing-only `shouldEmitPuckFix` when stopped
- **Driving tile prefetch:** `configureDrivingTilePrefetch()` after style load — `prefetchZoomDelta=3`, `setMaximumAmbientCacheSize(256MB)`; `DrivingTilePrefetcher` warms ambient cache via `putResourceWithUrl(url, bytes, modified, expires, etag, mustRevalidate)` on IO — MapLibre **11.5.1** has no callback overload; bearing-biased extra top padding in `computeDrivingViewportPadding()` when speed > 2 m/s
- Road-snap puck: `snapLocationToRoute()` projects GPS onto nearest `routeGeometryPoints` segment when within `SNAP_TO_ROUTE_MAX_M = 18f` m (release `22f`); `applyAndroidLocation()` uses snapped `displayLocation` for puck/HUD/`lastKnownLocation` but passes **raw** `locationWithBearing` to both `evaluateStepAdvancement()` and `updateRouteProgress()` so off-route (35 m) and greying stay honest on parallel streets; helper `closestPointOnSegment()` returns `ClosestSegmentResult(distM, lat, lng)` — do not use `distanceToSegmentMeters()` alone for snap (it discards the projected coordinates)
- Driving smoothness (2026-06): `isDuplicateLocationFix()` dedupes GPS; `applyDrivingTrackingPadding()` caches `lastAppliedTrackingPadding`; `maybeUpdateUiStateCoords()` throttles lat/lng (1 s / 20 m); `updateRouteProgress()` skips map GeoJSON rebuild until ≥10 m; `activateFreeDriveTrackingMode()` only when not already `TRACKING_GPS` + `RenderMode.GPS`
- Free drive `applyAndroidLocation()`: do NOT call `forceLocationUpdate()` — LocationEngine feeds puck; manual `pushPuckLocationIfNeeded(force=true)` only via `forceLocationUpdateForImmediateRender()` after padding/layout changes
- Puck centers on screen after minimizing/reopening during free-drive or nav: `MainActivity.onResume()` → `retryLocationActivation()` re-runs `activateLocationTracking()` on **every** resume; `applyDrivingTrackingPadding()`'s own dedup cache (`lastAppliedTrackingPadding`/`lastEngagedTrackingPadding`) sees no key change and skips re-pushing `paddingWhileTracking`, so a native-side padding reset across pause/resume sticks — `activateLocationTracking()` calls `invalidateDrivingPaddingCache()` before `applyDrivingTrackingPadding(map)` so the Map Settings puck offset is force-reapplied on every resume; also only calls `createLocationEngine(ctx)` on first activation (reuses `this.locationEngine` on repeat activation) so bearing/smoothing state isn't discarded each resume
- Remember passed places (`EncounteredPlacesRepository`, `data/places/`): Map Settings **Remember passed places** toggle gates GPS-based sampling (200 m / 30 s throttle, Logcat tag `EncounteredPlaces`) into `filesDir/places/encountered.db`; nav corridor sampling uses Overture only, free drive also samples vector POIs at zoom ≥ 15; **Clear passed places** deletes all rows; toggling OFF stops new writes but keeps existing rows
- Speed readout: `SpeedCircle` in `CarMapViewContainer.kt` — bottom-center **54dp** circle, **4dp** above map bottom (`SpeedCircleBottomInset`); cyan speed number (17sp) + dimmed `km/h` (10sp); always visible (including 0); do NOT reattach to puck or use `puckScreenX/Y`
- Do NOT replace default MapLibre GPS puck with custom `gpsName` bitmap for speed — bearing wedge is required; use bottom-center `SpeedCircle` Compose overlay instead
- Free-drive map HUD: top-left panel in `CarMapViewContainer` renders **only when `isNavigating`** — no "Free Drive" / "Scanning Road..." placeholder; nav street + turn/distance rows unchanged

## Camera modes (free drive / nav / top-down)

- After OSRM route draw, `RouteOverviewController.showRouteThenDive()` shows a 2 s `LatLngBounds` overview then dives to `CameraMode.TRACKING_GPS` (zoom 17.5, tilt 55°) — do not set `TRACKING` immediately after route draw or it snaps back before the dive
- `startFreeDrive()` removes route layer/source, resets `MapUiState`, snaps once via `snapCameraToGpsIfNeeded()` — do not re-snap on every GPS fix (causes camera twitching)
- Free drive camera: `FREE_DRIVE_ZOOM` 17.5 / default tilt **40°** (`driving_tilt` pref, slider 20–60°) / `CameraMode.TRACKING_GPS`; full nav uses zoom 18.5 / tilt **free-drive + NAV_TILT_OFFSET** (default 40° + 15° = **55°**)
- **Dynamic nav zoom:** while `isNavigating` and following (`!isCameraDetached`, not route overview / nav dive transition), `NavigationZoom.targetZoomForManeuverDistance()` maps puck→next-maneuver distance to zoom in `[15, navZoom]` (log curve; ≤80 m = ceiling, ≥1.5 km = floor); applied via `LocationComponent.zoomWhileTracking()` from `evaluateStepAdvancement()` — **not** during `enterNavigationCamera()` handshake; 0.2 zoom hysteresis; `setDrivingZoom()` updates ceiling only; reset in `startFreeDrive()` via `resetDynamicNavigationZoom()`
- One-time snap: `hasSnappedCameraToGps` gates `snapCameraToGpsIfNeeded()`; use `moveCamera` then `TRACKING_GPS` — do not loop animated `setCameraMode` or stale-target checks on GPS updates
- Style-load callback calls `startFreeDrive()` after `activateLocationTracking()`; `retryLocationActivation()` must NOT call `startFreeDrive()` again (duplicate snap/twitch)
- Enabling `CameraMode.TRACKING` at wide fallback zoom (6) locks the visual view zoomed out even when `cameraPosition.zoom` reports 14–16 — snap after location component is active
- End navigation button in `CarMapViewContainer` (Close icon, red tint) calls `engine.startFreeDrive()` when `isNavigating`
- 3D nav camera: `RouteOverviewController.showRouteThenDive()` sets `CameraMode.NONE` + `cancelTransitions()`, animates bounds in `ROUTE_OVERVIEW_ANIMATION_MS` (2 s), holds full-route view for `ROUTE_OVERVIEW_HOLD_MS` (10 s) with `routeOverviewProgress` timer bar in `CarMapViewContainer`; then `enterNavigationCamera()` — guard with `_uiState.value.isNavigating`; cancel overview in `startFreeDrive()` via `RouteOverviewController.clearRouteOverviewState()`
- Nav dive camera: `enterNavigationCamera()` must NOT call `zoomWhileTracking`/`tiltWhileTracking` right after `TRACKING_GPS` — MapLibre ignores them while camera mode is transitioning; use `CameraMode.NONE` → `map.animateCamera(zoom 18.5 / tilt 63°)` → set `TRACKING_GPS` in `CancelableCallback.onFinish` (same snap pattern as free drive)
- Manual pan/zoom sets `isCameraDetached` via `MapLibreMap.OnCameraMoveStartedListener.REASON_API_GESTURE`; recenter button in `CarMapViewContainer` `MapToolbarOverlay` shows when `isCameraDetached` (**including during navigation** — `GpsFixed` below red End nav); CropFree top-down button remains **free-drive only** (`!isNavigating`); tap calls `engine.recenterCamera()` → `enterNavigationCamera()` when navigating
- Free-drive camera follow regression: `applyDrivingTrackingPadding()` must NOT call `applyMapPaddingImmediate()` / `moveCamera(paddingTo)` while `component.cameraMode == TRACKING_GPS` — MapLibre drops out of follow mode; update `paddingWhileTracking` only; skip `forceLocationUpdateForImmediateRender()` while `shouldSmoothPuckMotion()` (padding-only update)
- After initial snap (`hasSnappedCameraToGps`), `applyAndroidLocation()` must call `activateFreeDriveTrackingMode()` on each GPS fix when `!isCameraDetached` — puck updates alone do not restore follow if tracking was lost
- `recenterCamera()` must clear `isInTopDownView` **before** `snapCameraToGpsIfNeeded()` — snap early-returns when top-down flag is still set
- `startFreeDrive()` and `recenterCamera()` must call `cancelTopDownViewportSync()` — stale `topDownViewportSyncRunnable` can force `CameraMode.NONE` after returning to free drive
- `dismissSelectedPoi()` must clear `isInTopDownView` — POI preview sets the flag via `focusOnPoi(moveCamera=true)` and leaving it set blocks free-drive follow permanently
- Top-view mode: `MapUiState.isInTopDownView` set by `animateTopDownCamera()` (flat tilt 0°, bearing 0°); distinct from `isCameraDetached` (manual pan also sets detached without top-down); cleared on `recenterCamera` / `snapCameraToGpsIfNeeded` / nav camera entry
- Top-view UI in `CarMapViewContainer`: when `isCameraDetached && !isInTopDownView && !isNavigating`, show CropFree `IconButton` only (no tooltip); top-right button `Column` must use `horizontalAlignment = Alignment.End` (not `CenterHorizontally`)
- Pin tap camera: `handleMapPointSelection()` calls `focusOnPoi(..., moveCamera = true)` → `animateTopDownCamera` at `POI_PREVIEW_ZOOM` (15.5); must `clearViewportPaddingForPreview()` via `paddingTo(0,0,0,0)` + zero `paddingWhileTracking` before animating — free-drive puck padding shifts POI off visual center; `handleMapLayoutChange()` re-centers on `selectedPoi` only when `isInTopDownView`; explore mode (no POI) calls `syncTopDownViewportPaddingOnly()` — do NOT recenter on `lastKnownLocation`; guard `applyDrivingViewportPadding` / `applyDrivingTrackingPadding` with `if (isInTopDownView) return`
- Top-view explore (CropFree): `TOP_DOWN_EXPLORE_ZOOM = 15.0`; `handleMapLayoutChange()` when `isInTopDownView` without `selectedPoi` → `syncTopDownViewportPaddingOnly()` only until `topDownExploreUserAdjusted`; user pan/zoom gesture cancels `topDownViewportSyncRunnable` + POI preview retries and sets `topDownExploreUserAdjusted`; `snapCameraToGpsIfNeeded()` / `activateFreeDriveTrackingMode()` / `applyAndroidLocation` must no-op camera moves when `isInTopDownView`; `clearPoiOverlay()` on `animateTopDownCamera()`; skip mix POI overlay refresh while `isInTopDownView` (native vector labels remain)
- Map pan stiffness (CropFree + free-drive manual pan): on `REASON_API_GESTURE` call `ensureTopDownCameraDetached()` and cancel dead reckoning for all modes; `topDownExploreUserAdjusted` skips `syncTopDownViewportPaddingOnly`/`scheduleTopDownViewportSync` after CropFree user pans; `applyDrivingTrackingPadding`/`activateFreeDriveTrackingMode`/`handleMapLayoutChange` bail when `isCameraDetached`; dead reckoning only when `!isInTopDownView && !isCameraDetached`
- Route overview after POI **Navigate**: `startNavigation()` must call `clearRoutePreviewState()` — cancel `pendingPoiPreviewTarget`, POI preview retries, and top-down viewport sync; clear `isInTopDownView` before `RouteOverviewController.showRouteThenDive()`; do NOT rely on `dismissSelectedPoi()` (Navigate calls `navigateToCoordinates()` directly)
- Route overview bounds: `fitRouteOverviewCamera()` uses full `routeGeometryPoints` via `buildRouteOverviewBounds()`; `handleMapLayoutChange()` re-fits while `routeOverviewJob?.isActive` only when `lastRouteOverviewLayoutWidth/Height` change (not every layout tick) — do not apply driving padding during overview (`isRouteOverviewActive()` guard in `applyDrivingTrackingPadding`); clear `lastAppliedTrackingPadding`/`lastEngagedTrackingPadding` on overview enter so puck offset re-applies after dive
- Nearby search main thread: `getNearbyPois()` → `currentViewportBounds()` uses `map.projection` (UI thread only) — `readOnMainThread()` dispatches from IO workers; `searchDestination()` already wraps viewport cache in `withContext(Dispatchers.Main)`
- Nav dive after overview: `navigationCameraTransitionActive` blocks `handleMapLayoutChange` and `applyDrivingTrackingPadding` while `enterNavigationCamera()` animates (2.5 s); post dive via `mapView.post { enterNavigationCamera() }` after 10 s hold; `activateNavigationTracking()` must snap to `navZoom`/`navTilt()` via `moveCamera` before `TRACKING_GPS` if animation was cancelled — otherwise nav HUD works but camera stays flat at overview zoom
- **Camera session / pan crash guard:** `NavigationCameraController.cameraSessionId` + `invalidateCameraSession()` — user pan/zoom (`REASON_API_GESTURE`), End nav (`startFreeDrive` → `prepareForFreeDriveCamera`), and `onDestroy()` must invalidate before re-engaging follow; always `map.cancelTransitions()` + `CameraMode.NONE` on those paths; `enterNavigationCamera()` captures session id at dive start — `CancelableCallback` and `activateNavigationTracking()` no-op when session stale, `!isNavigating`, or `isCameraDetached`; style/map writes use `mapReleased` + `withMapStyle` (`style.isFullyLoaded`) in `MapLibreEngineImpl`

## Viewport padding / puck position

- Waze-style puck: `applyDrivingViewportPadding()` — fraction-based pixel padding (`VIEWPORT_PADDING_LEFT_FRACTION=0.3`, `VIEWPORT_PADDING_TOP_FRACTION=0.4` of map view px dimensions) positions puck at ~65% from left and ~70% from top; uses `map.width`/`map.height` so it scales correctly across all screen sizes and densities; called from `activateLocationTracking()` and `applyFreeDriveToMap()`
- Puck position sliders: flow through `setViewportPadding()` → `applyPuckPaddingUpdate()` — while `TRACKING_GPS`, update `paddingWhileTracking` only (skip `applyDrivingViewportPadding` / `moveCamera(paddingTo)`); `handleMapLayoutChange` compares padding key before reapply (no unconditional cache clear); slider force uses `allowDuringSmoothing=true`; if follow lost, `activateNavigationTracking()` restores `TRACKING_GPS`
- Puck size slider: `puckScale` (default 1.0) controlled via `LocationComponentOptions.maxZoomIconScale` / `minZoomIconScale` + `locationComponent.applyStyle(updated)` — use `toBuilder()` on `component.locationComponentOptions` to preserve other options; `setPuckScale(scale)` is style-only — do NOT call `forceLocationUpdateForImmediateRender()` for scale (causes camera jolt in `TRACKING_GPS`; unlike viewport padding, scale does not need camera reposition); slider uses `onValueChange = onPuckScaleChange` only — do NOT use `onValueChangeFinished` with captured `puckScale` param (stale closure reverts tap/skip before recomposition)
- `applyDrivingTrackingPadding`: call `paddingWhileTracking` only via `applyPaddingWhileTrackingIfEngaged()` when `cameraMode != NONE`; when not yet `TRACKING_GPS`, use `moveCamera(paddingTo)` only and store intent in `lastAppliedTrackingPadding` — re-apply on `TRACKING_GPS` via `lastEngagedTrackingPadding` (`activateNavigationTracking` / `activateFreeDriveTrackingMode`); `activateLocationTracking` should call `applyDrivingTrackingPadding` (not `applyDrivingViewportPadding`) on style load; do NOT call `paddingWhileTracking` in `fitRouteOverviewCamera()` (overview is `CameraMode.NONE` + zero map padding only)
- **Top-view exit puck offset restore:** `clearViewportPaddingForPreview()` zeros map padding and clears `lastAppliedTrackingPadding`/`lastEngagedTrackingPadding` + `lastPaddingMapWidth/Height` — cannot clear `paddingWhileTracking` while `CameraMode.NONE`; `recenterCamera()` must call `scheduleFreeDrivePaddingRestore()` (`mapView.post` → `applyPuckPaddingUpdate`) after snap; `snapCameraToGpsIfNeeded` must `forceLocationUpdateForImmediateRender(allowDuringSmoothing=true)` after `applyDrivingTrackingPadding`; `activateFreeDriveTrackingMode` must re-apply padding when already `TRACKING_GPS` but `lastEngagedTrackingPadding == null` (do not early-return) — especially after full-map layout resize
- `computeDrivingViewportPadding` fallback: when `map.width == 0`, use `displayMetrics.widthPixels` / `heightPixels` with the user's fraction fields — never hardcode dp values in the fallback or the slider positions will be silently ignored before layout
- Map padding: use `CameraUpdateFactory.paddingTo()` via `applyMapPaddingImmediate()` — lazy `setPadding()` leaves viewport mismatched with MapView size (partial blank tiles in top-view); `scheduleTopDownViewportSync()` re-applies zero padding only on next frame — do NOT re-apply stored target/zoom (breaks free pan in top-view)
- POI preview camera: `schedulePoiPreviewCameraRetry()` + `moveCamera` (not `animateCamera`); `CarMapEngine.onMapHostLayoutChanged()` from `CarMapViewContainer.onSizeChanged` + `LaunchedEffect(activePanel, effectiveMapMediaRatio, selectedPoi)` in `DashboardScreen.kt`

## Route rendering / progress

- Route line vanishing on raster style: `ensureRouteLayers()` adds traveled/remaining layers above anchor (`osm`/traffic) — do not use plain `addLayer()` or line renders under tiles
- Puck vs traffic/route z-order: `LocationComponentOptions.layerAbove()` only applies at **`activateLocationComponent()`** — calling `applyStyle()` with `layerAbove` afterward does **not** move puck layers; do not rely on `ensurePuckAboveOverlays()` to fix overlays added later. Instead use `addLayerBelowPuckOrAbove()` / `findPuckAnchorLayerId()` (`LocationComponentConstants.*` in `PUCK_LAYER_IDS`) to insert overlays **below** the bottom-most puck layer. Vector Liberty style has no `RASTER_BASE_LAYER_ID` — plain `style.addLayer()` on traffic appends above the puck; `applyTrafficOverlay()` must use the puck-below helper, not raster-only `addLayerAbove(..., RASTER_BASE_LAYER_ID)`
- Route line styling: traveled/remaining split — grey `#6B7280` (`ROUTE_TRAVELED_*` layers) for passed segment, cyan `#00CBD6` (`ROUTE_REMAINING_*`) ahead; `updateRouteProgress()` on raw GPS with freeze while `distToRoute > ON_ROUTE_PROGRESS_MAX_M` (25 m) and on-route resync ≤ `ON_ROUTE_RESYNC_M` (18 m) after detours; route layers stack above traffic via `restackRouteLayersAbove()` / `ensureRouteLayers()` anchor
- Route line width: `ROUTE_WIDTH` 14f with casing 18f `#CC000000` below each line half; remove all four route layers + two sources in `applyFreeDriveToMap()` via `removeRouteLayers()`
- **Automotive road widths:** bundled `mix-auto-driving.json` (zoom-relative **2.75× / 3.1×** via `tools/gen_mix_auto_driving_style.py`) + runtime `applyAutomotiveRoadBoost()` (`AUTOMOTIVE_MAIN_ROAD_EXTRA` **1.55×** / `AUTOMOTIVE_MINOR_ROAD_EXTRA` **1.65×**); **split zoom ramps** — stock Liberty at z below start, full boost at z≥17: main `MAIN_BOOST_ZOOM_START` / `AUTOMOTIVE_MAIN_BOOST_ZOOM_START` **13**, minor `MINOR_BOOST_ZOOM_START` / `AUTOMOTIVE_MINOR_BOOST_ZOOM_START` **15** (`isAutomotiveMinorRoadLineLayer()` / `road_boost_zoom_start()`); `BOOST_ZOOM_FULL` / `AUTOMOTIVE_BOOST_ZOOM_FULL` **17**; regenerate JSON after changing factors or zoom constants in script

## Style / chrome / traffic overlay

- TomTom traffic overlay: `LauncherPreferences.showTraffic` + `tomTomApiKey`; `MapLibreEngineImpl.applyTrafficOverlay()` adds `RasterSource` via `TileSet("2.1.0", url)` (not direct URL constructor — `{z}/{x}/{y}` placeholder bug); layer IDs `mix-traffic-source` / `mix-traffic-layer`; Orbis v2 URL `https://api.tomtom.com/maps/orbis/traffic/flow/raster/tile/{z}/{x}/{y}?apiVersion=2&key={KEY}&style=light&tileSize=256` — valid styles **`light`** and **`dark`** only
- MapLibre chrome (`MapLibreEngineImpl.configureMapUiChrome()`): compass **bottom-right**; logo + attribution **bottom-left**; `setAttributionMargins` left must be **92 dp** (`ATTRIBUTION_LEFT_MARGIN_DP` / SDK `maplibre_ninety_two_dp`) — uniform 8 dp margins overlap ℹ on MapLibre logo text; MapLibre logo optional (`setLogoEnabled(false)`) but OSM/data attribution still required visibly
- MapLibre logo vs attribution ℹ spacing: `configureMapUiChrome()` sets `setAttributionMargins` left inset via **`ATTRIBUTION_LEFT_MARGIN_DP = 98f`** (MapLibre logo ~92 dp + 6 dp gap) — increase if watermark and ℹ still touch on device
- MapLibre compass default top-right overlaps destination search icon — `MapLibreEngineImpl.configureCompassPosition()` sets `uiSettings.setCompassGravity(Gravity.BOTTOM or Gravity.END)` with `COMPASS_MARGIN_DP` (16f) margins on style load
- Map toolbar layout (`CarMapViewContainer.kt`): **top-center** = `DestinationSearchFab` (circle, `PrimaryTapTarget` 84 dp, 40 dp icon, `CircleShape`, cyan active); **top-end** = `MapToolbarOverlay` (End nav when navigating, recenter when `isCameraDetached`, CropFree when detached free-drive only — no search); **bottom-start** = `MapSettingsFab` only (`ActivePanel.MAP_DATA` toggle); use `PanelHeaderTapTarget` (48 dp) + `MapLibreAttributionReserveDp` (40 dp bottom padding) so map-settings FAB sits above logo/ℹ row — do NOT keep map settings in top-right stack
- Map settings FAB (`MapSettingsFab` in `CarMapViewContainer.kt`, bottom-start above attribution): use single **`Icons.Filled.Layers`** — do NOT composite Map + Edit badges; active state matches destination search (cyan bg + black icon when `ActivePanel.MAP_DATA` open)
- Vector tiles: `LauncherPreferences.useVectorTiles` (default **true** on first launch) → `CarMapEngine.setMapStyle()`; raster OSM JSON vs OpenFreeMap Liberty `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty`
- 3D buildings toggle: `LauncherPreferences.show3dBuildings` (key `show_3d_buildings`, default **false** on first launch) → `LauncherViewModel.toggleShow3dBuildings()` → `CarMapEngine.setShow3dBuildings()` → `MapLibreEngineImpl.apply3dBuildingVisibility(style)` iterates `style.layers` and sets `Property.NONE`/`Property.VISIBLE` on every `FillExtrusionLayer`; called on style load AND on toggle; toggle is disabled (38% alpha) in `SettingsSwitchRow` when vector tiles is off

## POI overlay / custom pins / map tap

- POI pin layer (`SymbolLayer`) must use `style.addLayerAbove(poiLayer, RASTER_BASE_LAYER_ID)` on first add — plain `style.addLayer()` renders the layer below the OSM raster tiles and pins become invisible; fall back to `addLayer()` only when `RASTER_BASE_LAYER_ID` is absent (vector style)
- POI map pins: camera-idle listener (zoom ≥ 13, 1.5 s debounce) loads local Overture bbox first then merges Photon; use `mergePoiPins()` not `mergeAndDeduplicate()` for pin layer — latter re-sorts by distance and evicts categorized local pins
- `PoiIconFactory.kt` generates category teardrop bitmaps (F/G/H/A/$/S/R/•); SymbolLayer uses data-driven `iconImage` from normalized Overture/Photon category
- Map tap anywhere: `MapLibreEngineImpl.addOnMapClickListener` — POI pin hit uses feature props; empty tap finds nearest `poiCache` entry within `MAP_TAP_NEAREST_POI_MAX_M` (500 m) or creates `SearchResultPlace("Dropped Pin", isDroppedPin=true)` with `formatLatLng` subtitle
- Starred map pins: `CarMapEngine.setSavedPlaces()` → `savedPlacesKeys` (lat/lng rounded 5 dp) → GeoJSON `starred` property → `poiCategoryIconExpression()` uses `Expression.switchCase` for gold `poi_icon_starred_*` icons from `PoiIconFactory`
- Custom pin drop: **long press only** via `addOnMapLongClickListener` in `MapLibreEngineImpl`; short tap uses `handleMapPointSelection()` (saved layer → custom pin layer → POI layer) — no draft on tap
- Custom pin long-press in free drive (`!isNavigating && !isCameraDetached`): `exitFreeDriveToTopViewIfNeeded()` → `animateTopDownCamera()` at drop lat/lng (tilt 0°, `CameraMode.NONE`, `isCameraDetached = true`); skip if user already manually detached camera
- Saved/starred custom pin tap: query `SAVED_PLACES_LAYER_ID` first; `focusOnPoi(..., moveCamera = true)` centers map on pin; `focusOnPoi()` calls `clearCustomPin()` when `isSavedPlace(place)` — gold ★ on saved layer only, no cyan `+` overlay
- Map pin hit test: use `isTapNearPinIcon()` screen-space radius (`MAP_PIN_ICON_HIT_RADIUS_DP = 38f` × density) — do NOT use geographic `findSavedPlaceAt(tapLat, tapLng)` fallback before drafting (50 m blocked new pins near saved pins)
- Custom pin draft blocked during active navigation (`isNavigating`) on long press
- Vector tile POI overlay pins: `queryTilePois()` must use `map.queryRenderedFeatures(screenBounds, *VECTOR_POI_LAYER_IDS)` with Liberty style layer IDs `poi_r1`, `poi_r7`, `poi_r20`, `poi_transit` — do NOT use `VectorSource.querySourceFeatures("poi")` (tile cache misses POIs already painted on screen)
- **Custom pin draft vs saved:** unsaved `isDroppedPin` → `placeCustomPin(..., pending = true)` only — **never** `pending = false` until starred; `startCustomPinDraft()` must NOT auto-commit after reverse geocode; `LauncherPreferences.savedPlaces` / star toggle is the **only** persist path — Confirm Add Place does not save; `setSavedPlaces()` clears custom pin when selected POI is saved, restores pending draft when unstarred during `POI_DETAIL`
- Saved-pin streaks on tilted driving camera: `SAVED_PLACES_LAYER_ID` and **`mix-poi-layer`** must use `poiIconOnlyLayerProperties()` (no `textField`) + `iconPitchAlignment(MAP)` — icon+text on same `SymbolLayer` triggers MapLibre #2788 streaks; labels go on separate **`mix-poi-label-layer`** (`poiTextOnlyLayerProperties`, `textPitchAlignment(VIEWPORT)`) visible only when `isCameraDetached && !isInTopDownView && !isNavigating && selectedPoi == null`; hide Liberty `poi_r*` when mix icon overlay active (show in top-down / POI preview / zoom < 13); exclude `savedPlacesKeys` from `mergePoiPins()`
- POI cache merge: `poiCacheKey` rounds lat/lng to 5 dp; `mergeIntoPoiCache` merges within 50 m via `preferPoiEntry` (priority overture > search > photon > vector); `sortPoiPinsForMerge` before overlay rebuild; `SearchResultPlace.poiSource` tags ingest
- Search preview not on map: `focusOnPoi` upserts `encountered.db` (`SOURCE_SEARCH`, always — not gated on remember toggle) + `mergeIntoPoiCache`; forced `mix-preview-poi-layer` + `mix-preview-poi-label-layer` during POI_DETAIL when `!isPlaceRenderedOnMap`

## Search origin / destination search

- Destination search distance: default **500 km** cap via `MAX_SEARCH_RADIUS_M` in `DestinationSearchCoordinator`; filter runs after `mergeAndDeduplicate()` when `limitDistance` is true — local SQLite bbox (±0.5°) unchanged
- Launcher Settings toggle **"Nearby results only (within 500 km)"** (`LauncherPreferences.limitSearchDistance`, default ON) flows DashboardScreen → CarMapViewContainer → NavigationSearchOverlay → `searchDestination(limitDistance)`; include `limitSearchDistance` in search `LaunchedEffect` keys so toggling re-queries
- Photon returns global results (lat/lon is bias only); public OSRM demo server cannot reliably route intercontinental or 5000+ km trips — distance limit protects search UX, not routing capability
- Search origin: `CarMapEngine.resolveSearchOrigin()` — GPS from `MapUiState` → `lastKnownLocation` → `resolveMapViewOriginForSearch()` (zoom ≥ 10, or **any zoom while navigating**) → system `readLastKnownLocation` → `DEFAULT_LOCATION` (PH center); **never `(0,0)`**; `isValidSearchOrigin()` rejects near-zero coords; `resolveInitialLocation()` must set `MapUiState.currentLat/currentLng` from cached fix on cold start
- Search origin refresh: `NavigationSearchContent` calls `engine.refreshSearchOrigin()` on open then **snapshots** `resolveSearchOrigin()` + `hasReliableSearchOrigin()` for the panel session — do NOT key typed-search or nearby `LaunchedEffect` on live `uiState.currentLat/Lng` (cancels Photon while driving); remount on close/reopen refreshes snapshot
- Search origin UX: `hasReliableSearchOrigin()` = GPS/last fix/camera (not PH default fallback); overlay shows **Waiting for GPS** when typed search empty and snapshot origin unreliable — not generic "No results found"
- Search diagnostics: `DestinationSearchCoordinator.searchDestination()` logs query, origin, local/cache/photon counts under tag `MapLibreEngineImpl`; `searchDestination()` / `getNearbyPois()` **honor valid passed lat/lng** — do not always override with live `resolveSearchOrigin()` when caller supplies snapshot coords
- Nearby search suggestions: `getNearbyPois()` offline ±0.5° bbox + full `poiCache` + **viewport** `poiCache` entries; `seedSearchFromMapViewport()` on search open loads tile/local POIs into cache; nearby UI limit **20**; `searchPoiCache` matches name/subtitle/category; typed search also uses `searchViewportPoiCache`
